issue: 220
title: a `skip` name the test rebinds is not pytest's skip
origin: issue #220 negative. the test's own binding shadows the import, as for a setup callback (tests/test_setup_phase_skips.py)
=== head: app/__init__.py ===

=== head: app/billing.py ===
def total(items):
    return round(sum(items), 2)
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from pytest import skip

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    assert total([50.0, 28.75]) == 78.75
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from pytest import skip

from app.billing import total


def test_total():
    skip = print; skip("flaky")
    assert total([50.0, 28.75]) == 78.75
